<div class='items'>A workshop on importance of Newspaper Reading was conducted on 8th May 2019, for classes V to X with an objective to encourage the young learners to develop the habit of reading a newspaper.</div>

<div class='items'>Social Science Department organised a special screening of the National award winning film, Newton, for class IX on 3rd May 2019 with twin objective: 1.To make students familiar with the role of election commission in conducting free and fair elections in India, 2. Importance of voting in a democrating country. </div>

<div class='items'>On 30th April 2019, MSMS celebrated the Grand Finale of its month long Mahavir Jayanti Celebrations on the theme 'Save Our Earth', promoting the values of non-voilence, empathy for living beings and love for all as espoused by Lord Mahavira. </div>

<div class='items'>Anshika Gupta of class VI-A and Riddhima Gupta of class V-A bagged the Second Prize in the Annual competitive event Saturnalia, held on 30.04.2019 at St.Margaret School, Derawal Nagar under the category of Poem Enactment Competition on topic Awaiting 2050. </div>

<div class='items'>Mahavir Senior Model School has once again clinched the prestigious International School Award 2018-2021, an award bestowed by British Council. </div>

